        "# **Codveda Task: Level 3**\n",
        "\n",
        "## Task 1: Sentiment Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "## **Project Overview**\n",
        "This project focuses on performing sentiment analysis on textual data to identify whether a text expresses a positive, negative, or neutral sentiment. The analysis applies Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques to clean and preprocess the text, including tokenization, stopword removal, and stemming. TextBlob is then used to calculate sentiment polarity and classify each text into a sentiment category. The results are visualized using sentiment distribution charts, word frequency analysis, and word clouds to identify common patterns and understand the overall sentiment expressed in the dataset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "##Dataset Description\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset contains 732 social media posts and related information used for sentiment analysis. The main text field, Text, contains the textual content analyzed to determine sentiment. The dataset also includes an existing Sentiment column, which provides sentiment labels for comparison with the sentiment predictions generated using TextBlob.\n",
        "\n",
        "Additional attributes include information such as user, platform, country, timestamp, hashtags, retweets, likes, and date/time-related features. These variables provide contextual information about the posts, while the primary focus of this project is the textual content.\n",
        "\n",
        "For the sentiment analysis, the Text column was cleaned and preprocessed through lowercasing, tokenization, stopword removal, and stemming. TextBlob was then applied to calculate polarity and classify each post as Positive, Negative, or Neutral."
      ],
